# Replay template — rendered from this template by scripts/record-themes.sh.
# It does NOT drive malt. The wrapper drives the CLI install and the mt tui
# dashboard inside tmux, polls the real screen until the content is right, and
# captures it to an ANSI dump. This tape just `cat`s that static dump so VHS
# renders it faithfully — truecolor and the reverse-video selection background,
# both of which freeze drops. Because the content is already settled, there is no
# timing to race: the capture is deterministic, the render is just a redraw.
#
# @PLACEHOLDERS@ are substituted per still before vhs runs.

Output "@SINK@"

Set Shell "bash"
Set FontSize 14
Set Width 1060
Set Height 820
Set Padding 16
Set Theme "@VHS_THEME@"
Set TypingSpeed 0ms

# Print the captured screen, then block on `sleep` so no shell prompt or cursor
# lands in the frame. VHS renders the redraw; we snapshot it.
Hide
Type "clear; cat '@ANSI@'; sleep 30"
Enter
Show
Sleep 700ms
Screenshot "@OUT@"
